### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure:** The dataset will follow a strict directory hierarchy: `image_generation_dataset/` containing subfolders for `images/` (organized by split), `metadata/` (containing JSONL files), and explicit `train/`, `validation/`, and `test/` directories to prevent data leakage. 

**Generation Strategy:** We will utilize a stratified sampling approach to ensure balanced representation across the 11 required visual categories. Prompts will be generated using a templated engine that randomizes subjects, styles, and environmental conditions while enforcing uniqueness constraints to avoid near-duplicates across splits. The split ratio will be strictly maintained at 80% Training, 10% Validation, and 10% Testing.

**Quality-Control Process:** Each entry will undergo automated validation to check for the presence of all 14 mandatory metadata fields. Semantic similarity checks (using CLIP embeddings) will be run across splits to ensure no near-duplicate images exist between training and evaluation sets. Human-in-the-loop verification will spot-check 5% of entries for prompt-image alignment and label accuracy.

