### Dataset Strategy Overview

**Structure:** The dataset will follow a hierarchical directory structure: `image_generation_dataset/` containing subdirectories for `images/` (organized by split), `metadata/` (containing JSONL files for each split), and explicit folders for `train/`, `validation/`, and `test/` to ensure logical separation. 

**Generation Strategy:** We will employ a stratified sampling approach to guarantee balanced representation across the 11 required categories. Prompts will be generated using a controlled vocabulary to prevent semantic drift, with a deduplication algorithm (MinHash LSH) applied to ensure no near-duplicate images leak between splits. The split ratio will be strictly enforced at 80% (Train), 10% (Validation), and 10% (Test).

**Quality-Control Process:** Each entry will undergo automated schema validation to ensure all 14 fields are present and correctly typed. A secondary semantic consistency check will verify that the `detailed image-generation prompt` aligns with the `main subject` and `tags`. Human-in-the-loop review will be simulated by flagging entries with generic descriptors (e.g., "nice image") for revision.

