### Dataset Development Plan: Text-to-Image Vision Dataset

#### 1. Proposed Dataset Structure
The dataset will utilize a hierarchical directory structure to ensure seamless integration into machine learning pipelines (e.g., PyTorch, TensorFlow). 
- **Root Directory:** `image_generation_dataset/`
  - `images/`: Raw generated images (PNG/JPG).
  - `metadata/`: JSONL files containing the 14 required metadata fields.
  - `train/`: Training split (80% of data).
  - `validation/`: Validation split (10% of data).
  - `test/`: Testing split (10% of data).

#### 2. Generation Strategy for Diversity
To prevent mode collapse and ensure a robust distribution across the 11 mandated categories (Human, Nature, Architecture, Animals, Objects, Food, Vehicles, Fantasy/Sci-Fi, Digital Art, Abstract, and Everyday Life), the following strategies will be applied:
- **Environment Matrix:** Subjects will be mapped against diverse environments (e.g., Urban, Wilderness, Futuristic, Domestic, Ethereal).
- **Lighting Scenarios:** A rotation of lighting conditions (e.g., Golden Hour, High-Contrast Noir, Diffused Overcast, Neon Cyberpunk, Volumetric Sunlight) will be applied across categories.
- **Balanced Category Sampling:** A strict quota system will ensure equal representation across all categories.

#### 3. Quality Control & Prompt Alignment
- **Semantic Verification:** Prompts will follow a "Subject → Action → Environment → Style" hierarchy to guarantee the model captures all attributes accurately.
- **Leakage Prevention:** A "Seed-Based Partitioning" method will group images with similar prompts via a shared seed-prefix, assigning them exclusively to one split to prevent near-duplicate leakage.
- **Attribute Validation:** Each entry will be cross-referenced against the 14 metadata fields to ensure the detailed generation prompt faithfully expands the short caption without misleading labels.

