### Data Curation Strategy for High-Fidelity Text-to-Image Datasets

#### 1. Proposed Data Structure and Split Strategy
To ensure seamless integration into machine learning pipelines, the dataset will utilize a hierarchical directory structure. The root folder, `image_generation_dataset/`, will contain `images/`, `metadata/`, `train/`, `validation/`, and `test/` directories. The dataset will be split as follows: 80% Training (high-variance samples for weight optimization), 10% Validation (for hyperparameter tuning), and 10% Testing (a hold-out set of unique compositions and edge cases). To prevent data leakage, perceptual hashing (pHash) will be implemented to ensure no near-duplicate images exist across splits.

#### 2. Generation Plan for Diversity
We will employ a matrix-based generation approach to prevent mode collapse and ensure robust generalization across balanced categories (humans, nature, architecture, animals, products, food, vehicles, sci-fi, digital art, abstract, and everyday life). 
- **Lighting Conditions:** Rotating through Golden Hour, High-Key studio, Low-Key cinematic, Volumetric fog/god rays, and Harsh Midday sun.
- **Artistic Styles:** Spanning Photorealism, Cyberpunk, Minimalist, Baroque, and Architectural Photography.

#### 3. Quality Control Metrics
Data cleanliness will be maintained through a rigorous pipeline:
- **CLIP Score:** To measure semantic alignment between generated images and detailed prompts.
- **Aesthetic Score:** Using a pre-trained aesthetic predictor to filter out low-compositional quality images.
- **Inception Score (IS) & FID:** To ensure diversity and quality of the generated distribution.
- **Label Fidelity:** Manual audits of batches to ensure main subject and secondary object fields are accurately described.

