### Proposed Dataset Framework

As an AI Dataset Engineer and Computer Vision Specialist, I have designed the following framework to ensure the dataset is robust, unbiased, and optimized for training high-fidelity text-to-image models.

#### 1. Dataset Structure & Hierarchy
The dataset will be organized to facilitate seamless integration into PyTorch/TensorFlow data loaders.
```text
image_generation_dataset/
├── images/                 # All raw image files (.jpg, .png)
├── metadata/               # Global metadata registry (JSONL)
├── train/                  # Training split pointers/manifests
├── validation/             # Validation split pointers/manifests
└── test/                   # Test split pointers/manifests
```

#### 2. Generation Strategy
To prevent mode collapse and ensure generalization, I will employ a **Stratified Diversity Matrix**. 
- **Category Balancing:** Each of the 11 required categories will be assigned an equal weight.
- **Attribute Permutation:** I will rotate lighting (Golden hour → Cinematic → Neon → Overcast), camera angles (Bird's eye → Macro → Low angle), and styles (Photorealistic → Impressionist → Digital Art) across the categories.
- **Prompt Engineering:** I will use a "Global-to-Local" prompting strategy: [Subject] → [Action/Pose] → [Environment] → [Lighting/Atmosphere] → [Technical Camera Specs] → [Artistic Style].

#### 3. Quality Control Process
- **Leakage Prevention:** A hashing mechanism will be used to ensure that no two images with similar visual compositions appear in different splits (e.g., the same subject in a different outfit will not be split between Train and Test).
- **Label Validation:** Each entry will be cross-referenced against a taxonomy of "forbidden" vague terms (e.g., "beautiful," "detailed") and replaced with descriptive technical terms (e.g., "intricate filigree," "hyper-realistic skin pores").
- **Resolution Consistency:** All entries will be mapped to specific aspect ratios to ensure the model learns spatial composition.

