### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure**: The dataset will follow a hierarchical directory structure: `image_generation_dataset/` containing `train/`, `validation/`, and `test/` subdirectories for images, and a unified `metadata/` folder for JSONL files. This ensures clear separation of splits for reproducible training and evaluation.

**Generation Strategy**: We will employ a stratified sampling approach to ensure balanced representation across the 11 required visual categories (portraits, nature, architecture, etc.). Prompts will be generated using a diverse lexicon of artistic styles, lighting conditions, and camera compositions to prevent model bias. To prevent near-duplicate leakage, we will apply perceptual hashing (pHash) with a strict threshold across the entire corpus before splitting; any image pair exceeding the similarity threshold will have one instance removed or significantly altered.

**Quality-Control Process**: Each entry undergoes a three-step validation: (1) Syntax check to ensure all 14 mandatory metadata fields are present and correctly typed; (2) Semantic consistency check to verify the prompt aligns with the caption and tags; (3) Split integrity audit to confirm the 80/10/10 distribution and absence of cross-split duplicates.

