### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure**: The dataset will follow a hierarchical directory structure: `image_generation_dataset/` containing subdirectories for `images/` (raw assets), `metadata/` (JSONL files), and split-specific folders (`train/`, `validation/`, `test/`) linking to unique image IDs. Each entry will strictly enforce the 14-field schema to ensure reproducibility.

**Generation Strategy**: We will employ a stratified sampling approach to guarantee balanced representation across the 11 defined visual categories. Prompts will be generated using a template-based system with randomized modifiers for style, lighting, and composition to prevent semantic drift. To ensure the 80/10/10 split integrity, we will apply perceptual hashing (pHash) with a Hamming distance threshold to detect and exclude near-duplicates across splits before final assignment.

**Quality-Control Process**: A two-stage QC pipeline will be implemented. First, automated scripts will validate JSON schema compliance, check for null fields, and verify aspect ratio/resolution consistency. Second, a human-in-the-loop review will sample 5% of each split to evaluate prompt-image alignment score and artistic coherence, flagging any ambiguous tags or redundant compositions for regeneration.

