### Repository Structure & Engineering Framework

**1. Repository Hierarchy**
```text
image_generation_dataset/
├── images/                 # Raw image assets (organized by category)
├── metadata/               # Master JSONL files containing all 14 fields
├── train/                  # 80% Split: image_id.jpg + corresponding metadata
├── validation/             # 10% Split: image_id.jpg + corresponding metadata
└── test/                   # 10% Split: image_id.jpg + corresponding metadata
```

**2. Prompt Generation Algorithm**
I utilize a **Combinatorial Attribute Matrix (CAM)**. Instead of random generation, I cross-reference a matrix of `[Subject] x [Environment] x [Lighting] x [Art Style]`. This ensures that "Cyberpunk" isn't only paired with "Cities," but also with "Nature" or "Food," preventing dataset bias and ensuring a balanced distribution across the 11 required categories.

**3. Validation Framework**
*   **Semantic De-duplication:** Using CLIP embeddings to ensure no two prompts in different splits are semantically identical or near-duplicate.
*   **Constraint Checklist:** A programmatic validator ensures every entry contains exactly 14 metadata fields and aligns with the target folder hierarchy.
*   **Diversity Audit:** A category-count check to ensure the 11 thematic pillars (human subjects, nature, architecture, animals, objects, food, vehicles, sci-fi/fantasy, digital art, abstract art, and everyday life) are represented equally.

