### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure:** The dataset will follow a hierarchical directory structure: `image_generation_dataset/` containing subdirectories `images/` (organized by split), `metadata/` (containing JSONL files), and explicit `train/`, `validation/`, and `test/` folders to prevent data leakage. 

**Generation Strategy:** We will employ a stratified sampling approach to ensure balanced representation across the 11 required visual categories. Prompts will be generated using a template-based system with randomized attributes for style, lighting, and composition to guarantee uniqueness. A deduplication algorithm based on semantic similarity (using CLIP embeddings) will be applied to ensure no near-duplicate images exist across splits.

**Quality-Control Process:** Each entry will undergo a three-stage validation: (1) Schema validation to ensure all 14 fields are present and correctly typed; (2) Semantic consistency check to verify the prompt matches the caption and tags; (3) Visual feasibility review to ensure prompts describe physically plausible scenes. 

