### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure & Hierarchy**: The dataset will follow the `image_generation_dataset/` root, segregating data into `train/` (80%), `validation/` (10%), and `test/` (10%) subdirectories. Each split will contain mirrored `images/` and `metadata/` folders to ensure clear separation of assets and annotations.

**Generation Strategy**: We will employ a stratified sampling approach to guarantee balanced representation across the 11 required categories (e.g., human subjects, nature, architecture). Prompts will be generated using a controlled vocabulary to prevent semantic drift, and a hashing algorithm will be applied to prompt embeddings to detect and eliminate near-duplicates across splits, preventing data leakage.

**Quality Control**: Every entry undergoes a three-step validation: (1) Schema validation to ensure all 14 metadata fields are present and correctly typed; (2) Semantic consistency checks to ensure the caption matches the detailed prompt; (3) Uniqueness verification to flag redundant compositions. Low-quality or ambiguous labels are automatically rejected.

