As an expert AI dataset engineer and computer vision specialist, I have designed a robust framework for building a high-quality text-to-image generation dataset. Below is the detailed methodology followed by the representative metadata samples.

### 1. Proposed Dataset Structure
The dataset will follow a hierarchical folder structure to ensure compatibility with standard training pipelines (e.g., PyTorch DataLoader, TensorFlow datasets):

```
image_generation_dataset/
├── images/
│   ├── train/
│   ├── validation/
│   └── test/
├── metadata/
│   ├── train_metadata.jsonl
│   ├── validation_metadata.jsonl
│   └── test_metadata.jsonl
```

**Split Strategy:**
- **Training (80%):** Diverse, high-variance samples used for model weight updates.
- **Validation (10%):** Held-out set for hyperparameter tuning and monitoring overfitting; strictly no near-duplicates from the training set.
- **Testing (10%):** Final evaluation set for benchmarking generative quality and prompt alignment; completely isolated from training and validation.

### 2. Generation Strategy
- **Prompt Engineering:** Prompts will be constructed using a modular template: `[Main Subject] + [Secondary Objects] + [Environment/Background] + [Art Style] + [Camera/Composition] + [Lighting] + [Color Palette]`. This ensures semantic richness and controllability.
- **Diversity Balancing:** We will enforce a stratified sampling approach across 11 key categories (Portraits, Nature, Architecture, Animals, Products, Food, Vehicles, Sci-Fi, Digital Art, Abstract, Everyday Life) to prevent category collapse.
- **Resolution Standardization:** All entries will target native resolutions compatible with modern diffusion models (e.g., 1024x1024, 1280x720), with aspect ratios explicitly tagged.

### 3. Quality-Control Process
- **Duplicate Detection:** Perceptual hashing (pHash) and CLIP embedding cosine similarity will be used to identify and remove near-duplicate images across all splits to prevent data leakage.
- **Semantic Alignment:** Each prompt-caption pair will be scored using a CLIP-based consistency metric; entries below a threshold of 0.85 will be flagged for manual review or regeneration.
- **Tag Verification:** Automated scripts will verify that all 14 required metadata fields are present and non-null.
- **Bias Mitigation:** Demographic attributes in human subjects will be balanced across gender, age, and ethnicity to ensure fair representation.

