**2. Generation Strategy**
- **Prompt Diversity**: We will utilize a stratified sampling approach across 11 core categories (Human Subjects, Nature, Architecture, Animals, Objects, Food, Vehicles, Fantasy, Digital Art, Abstract, Everyday Life) to ensure balanced representation.
- **Split Integrity**: A hash-based deduplication process will be applied to the semantic embedding of prompts before assignment. Images will be assigned to splits (80/10/10) only after confirming that no near-duplicate prompts exist in other splits, preventing data leakage.
- **Resolution & Aspect Ratio**: Resolutions will vary (e.g., 512x512, 768x1024, 1024x768) to train robust multi-scale models, with aspect ratios explicitly tagged.

**3. Quality-Control Process**
- **Automated Filtering**: Scripts will verify the presence of all 14 metadata fields and check for format consistency (e.g., valid hex codes for color palettes, correct float formats for resolution).
- **Semantic Validation**: A CLIP-based similarity check will flag any train/validation/test entries with a cosine similarity > 0.95 to ensure split purity.
- **Manual Spot-Check**: A random 1% sample from each category and split will be reviewed for prompt-image alignment and artistic coherence.

