### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

As an expert AI dataset engineer, I propose the following framework for constructing a high-fidelity text-to-image dataset:

**1. Dataset Structure & Folder Hierarchy**
The dataset will adhere to a modular directory structure to facilitate efficient loading and version control:
```
image_generation_dataset/
├── images/
│   ├── train/
│   ├── validation/
│   └── test/
└── metadata/
    ├── train.jsonl
    ├── validation.jsonl
    └── test.jsonl
```
This separation ensures that model training, hyperparameter tuning, and final evaluation are conducted on strictly disjoint data subsets, preventing data leakage.

**2. Generation Strategy**
We will employ a stratified sampling approach to ensure balance across 11 distinct visual categories: Human Subjects, Nature, Architecture, Animals, Objects, Food, Vehicles, Fantasy/Sci-Fi, Digital Art, Abstract, and Everyday Life. Prompts will be synthesized using a template-based system that varies subjects, styles, lighting, and compositions to maximize diversity. We will enforce an 80% (Training), 10% (Validation), and 10% (Testing) split ratio. Near-duplicate detection algorithms (e.g., perceptual hashing) will be run prior to splitting to ensure no semantically similar images appear in multiple sets.

**3. Quality-Control Process**
- **Schema Validation:** Automated scripts will verify that every entry contains all 14 mandatory metadata fields.
- **Prompt Diversity:** NLP analysis will check for lexical variety to prevent mode collapse during model training.
- **Visual Consistency:** A subset of generated prompts will be visually verified against their tags to ensure alignment (e.g., ensuring "night" lighting matches the "color palette").
- **Format Compliance:** All outputs will be strictly formatted as JSONL for stream processing compatibility.

