### Structural Design
The dataset follows a hierarchical directory structure rooted at `image_generation_dataset/`. Subdirectories include `images/` for master assets, `metadata/` for central JSONL records, and split-specific folders `train/`, `validation/`, and `test/` containing 80%, 10%, and 10% of the images respectively. This clear separation prevents data leakage and overfitting.

### Generation Strategy
To ensure high-fidelity text-to-image pairs, a Multi-Dimensional Prompting Framework is employed. Prompts are engineered using a modular template: [Subject] + [Action/State] + [Environment] + [Style] + [Lighting/Atmosphere] + [Technical Specs]. A cross-category diversity matrix ensures the dataset spans all 11 required categories without clustering around common AI tropes, intentionally including extreme angles and varied focal lengths.

### Quality Control Measures
Quality control involves automated checks for unique IDs, non-empty fields, and valid resolution formats. Perceptual hashing of images and prompt embeddings ensures no two entries share excessive semantic similarity, strictly preventing near-duplicates from leaking across splits. Manual review protocols flag ambiguous captions, and strict adherence to the 14-field metadata schema ensures downstream compatibility with CLIP-style encoders.

