**Structure & Generation Strategy:**
The dataset will be organized into a root directory `image_generation_dataset/` with subdirectories for `images/` (raw assets), `metadata/` (centralized index), and split-specific folders (`train/`, `validation/`, `test/`) containing the respective JSONL manifest files. The generation strategy employs a stratified sampling approach to ensure the 80/10/10 split maintains distributional balance across all 11 visual categories. To prevent data leakage, a cryptographic hash of each prompt's semantic embedding will be computed; any near-duplicate exceeding a 0.95 cosine similarity threshold will be discarded or reassigned to ensure distinctness across splits.

**Quality-Control Process:**
1. **Schema Validation:** Automated scripts will verify the presence and type of all 14 required metadata fields for every entry.
2. **Semantic Diversity Check:** A clustering algorithm will analyze prompts within each split to ensure broad coverage of artistic styles and lighting conditions, flagging redundant compositions.
3. **Human-in-the-Loop Review:** A random 5% sample from each split will undergo manual audit for hallucination checks and label accuracy before final release.

