### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure**: The dataset will follow a hierarchical folder structure: `image_generation_dataset/` containing subdirectories for `images/` (organized by split), `metadata/` (containing JSONL files for each split), and explicit `train/`, `validation/`, and `test/` directories to enforce the 80/10/10 split. 

**Generation Strategy**: We will employ a stratified sampling approach across 11 distinct visual categories to ensure balance. Prompts will be generated using a template-based system that randomizes subjects, styles, and lighting while enforcing uniqueness constraints to prevent semantic duplication. 

**Quality Control**: A two-stage filtering process will be applied. First, an automated script will check for exact string matches in prompts and duplicate image IDs. Second, a semantic similarity check (using CLIP embeddings) will flag near-duplicate concepts across splits to prevent data leakage. All entries will be validated against the 14-field schema before ingestion.

