### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure & Generation Strategy:**
The dataset will be structured to support reproducible generative model training. We will employ a stratified sampling approach to ensure balanced representation across the 11 required visual categories (e.g., portraits, landscapes, sci-fi). The generation strategy involves creating unique, high-fidelity prompts that vary in complexity and stylistic descriptors to prevent model overfitting on specific phrasing patterns. 

**Quality-Control Process:**
1. **Uniqueness Check:** Automated semantic similarity scoring (using CLIP embeddings) will flag and remove near-duplicate prompts across splits to prevent data leakage.
2. **Metadata Validation:** A schema validator will ensure all 14 required fields are present and correctly typed for every entry.
3. **Split Integrity:** Scripts will verify the 80/10/10 distribution and confirm that no image IDs or semantically identical prompts exist in more than one split.
4. **Path Alignment:** All file paths will be programmatically checked to match the `image_generation_dataset/` hierarchy.

