## Dataset Engineering Strategy

As a senior AI researcher specializing in generative models, I propose the following framework for constructing this text-to-image dataset:

### 1. Dataset Structure & Folder Hierarchy
The dataset will follow a modular directory structure to facilitate efficient loading and splitting during model training:
```
image_generation_dataset/
├── images/
│   ├── train/       (80% of total images)
│   ├── validation/  (10% of total images)
│   └── test/        (10% of total images)
└── metadata/
    ├── train.jsonl
    ├── validation.jsonl
    └── test.jsonl
```

### 2. Generation Strategy
- **Diversity Sampling**: We will use a stratified sampling approach to ensure balanced representation across the 11 required categories (portraits, landscapes, architecture, etc.).
- **Prompt Engineering**: Prompts will be constructed using a template-based system that randomly combines subjects, styles, lighting, and camera parameters to maximize variation while maintaining semantic coherence.
- **Split Integrity**: To prevent data leakage, we will employ perceptual hashing (pHash) and semantic embedding clustering (using CLIP) to identify and remove near-duplicates before assigning splits. No image or its near-duplicate will appear in more than one split.

### 3. Quality-Control Process
- **Automated Validation**: A script will verify that every entry contains all 14 mandatory fields and that file paths exist.
- **Semantic Consistency Check**: We will run a preliminary inference pass with a robust captioning model to ensure the generated prompt aligns with the visual content described in the caption.
- **Human-in-the-Loop**: A random 5% sample from each category will be manually reviewed for artistic merit and label accuracy.

