### Proposed Dataset Strategy

**1. Dataset Structure:**
The dataset will follow a hierarchical folder structure: `image_generation_dataset/` containing subdirectories for `images/` (raw assets), `metadata/` (JSONL files), and split-specific folders (`train/`, `validation/`, `test/`). This ensures clear separation of concerns and reproducible loading pipelines.

**2. Generation Strategy:**
We will employ a stratified sampling approach to ensure balanced representation across 11 diverse visual categories (from portraits to abstract art). Prompts will be generated using a template-based system that randomly combines subjects, styles, lighting, and camera angles to minimize bias. We will enforce an 80/10/10 split (Training/Validation/Testing) with strict hashing checks to prevent near-duplicate leakage across splits.

**3. Quality-Control Process:**
Each entry undergoes a three-stage QC: (a) Automated schema validation to ensure all 14 required metadata fields are present; (b) Semantic consistency checks to verify the prompt aligns with the caption and tags; (c) Human-in-the-loop review for a random 5% sample to assess artistic coherence and label accuracy. Low-quality or ambiguous entries will be flagged for regeneration.

