### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

As an AI dataset engineer specializing in multimodal models, I propose the following framework for constructing a robust text-to-image generation dataset:

**1. Dataset Structure & Folder Hierarchy**
The dataset will follow a standardized directory structure to ensure compatibility with common training pipelines:
```
image_generation_dataset/
├── images/
│   ├── train/
│   ├── validation/
│   └── test/
└── metadata/
    ├── train.jsonl
    ├── validation.jsonl
    └── test.jsonl
```

**2. Generation Strategy**
- **Diversity:** We will curate prompts spanning 11 balanced categories: human portraits, nature, architecture, animals, products, food, vehicles, sci-fi/fantasy, digital art, abstract, and everyday life.
- **Splitting:** Data will be partitioned into 80% Training, 10% Validation, and 10% Testing. Strict deduplication algorithms (based on perceptual hash and prompt embedding similarity) will ensure no near-duplicate images leak across splits.
- **Prompt Engineering:** Prompts will be constructed to explicitly define subject, style, lighting, composition, and camera parameters to maximize model controllability.

**3. Quality-Control Process**
- **Automated Filtering:** Scripts will verify that all 14 required metadata fields are present and non-null for every entry.
- **Consistency Checks:** Aspect ratios and resolutions will be validated against the specified constraints.
- **Semantic Alignment:** A VQA (Visual Question Answering) model will sample entries to ensure the generated prompt aligns semantically with the caption and tags.

