### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure & Generation Strategy**:
I will construct a stratified dataset ensuring equal representation across the 11 specified visual categories. The generation strategy involves creating unique semantic seeds for each category to prevent conceptual drift. We will enforce a strict 80/10/10 split at the category level to maintain distribution balance across Training, Validation, and Testing sets. File naming conventions will follow the pattern `{split}_{category}_{unique_id}.png` to align with the `image_generation_dataset/` hierarchy.

**Quality-Control Process**:
1. **Semantic Uniqueness Check**: Embedding-based similarity scoring will be applied to all generated prompts to ensure no near-duplicates exist across splits.
2. **Schema Validation**: Automated scripts will verify the presence and type of all 14 required metadata fields.
3. **Visual Diversity Audit**: Manual review of a random sample from each split to confirm distinct camera angles, lighting conditions, and artistic styles.

