### Dataset Strategy Overview

As an AI dataset engineer specializing in diffusion models, my approach prioritizes semantic diversity, metadata fidelity, and strict split isolation to prevent data leakage.

**1. Dataset Structure & Folder Hierarchy**
The dataset will follow a standardized directory layout to ensure reproducibility:
```
image_generation_dataset/
├── images/
│   ├── train/
│   ├── validation/
│   └── test/
└── metadata/
    ├── train.jsonl
    ├── validation.jsonl
    └── test.jsonl
```

**2. Generation Strategy**
- **Prompt Engineering**: We will use a template-based generation system that randomizes subjects, styles, and lighting conditions while maintaining grammatical coherence. Prompts will be constructed to maximize CLIP score potential.
- **Category Balancing**: The generator will enforce a uniform distribution across 11 core categories (Portraits, Nature, Architecture, etc.) to prevent model bias.
- **Split Allocation**: Data will be partitioned into 80% Training, 10% Validation, and 10% Testing. Hash-based deduplication will be applied across splits to ensure no near-duplicate images leak between sets.

**3. Quality-Control Process**
- **Automated Filtering**: Scripts will verify that all 14 required metadata fields are present and non-null.
- **Semantic Consistency**: A secondary VLM (Vision-Language Model) will validate that the generated caption aligns with the prompt intent.
- **Uniqueness Check**: Perceptual hashing (pHash) will identify and remove redundant compositions.

