## Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure**: The dataset follows a hierarchical folder structure: `image_generation_dataset/` containing subdirectories `images/`, `metadata/`, `train/`, `validation/`, and `test/`. Images are stored in `images/` with unique UUIDs, while metadata JSONL files are split into the respective train/val/test folders.

**Generation Strategy**: We will use a stratified sampling approach to ensure balanced representation across 11 core categories (Portraits, Nature, Architecture, Wildlife, Products, Food, Vehicles, Sci-Fi, Digital Art, Abstract, Everyday Life). Prompts are generated using a template-based system that randomizes subject, style, lighting, and composition variables to prevent mode collapse. Near-duplicate detection (using perceptual hashing) will be run prior to splitting to ensure no data leakage between sets.

**Quality Control**: Each entry undergoes a three-step validation: (1) Schema completeness check (all 14 fields present), (2) Semantic consistency verification (caption matches prompt intent), and (3) Diversity scoring to ensure no redundant compositions. Only entries passing all checks are ingested.

