### Dataset Engineering Strategy & Quality Control

As an expert AI dataset engineer, I propose the following framework for building this high-quality text-to-image generation dataset:

**1. Dataset Structure:**
The dataset will follow a hierarchical directory structure rooted at `image_generation_dataset/`:
- `images/`: Stores raw/generated assets (referenced by ID).
- `metadata/`: Contains the master JSONL files.
- `train/`, `validation/`, `test/`: Subdirectories containing split-specific JSONL manifests and symlinks or copies of corresponding images.

**2. Generation Strategy:**
- **Prompt Engineering:** We will use a template-based approach combined with LLM variation to ensure diverse phrasing while maintaining strict adherence to the 14-field schema. Prompts will be seeded from curated concept lists for each of the 11 required categories to ensure balance.
- **Split Allocation:** We will generate entries and assign splits immediately: 80% Training, 10% Validation, 10% Testing. 
- **Deduplication:** To prevent leakage, we will compute perceptual hashes (pHash) and semantic text embeddings for every generated prompt. Any entry with a similarity score >0.95 to an existing entry in a different split will be discarded or reassigned to the same split.

**3. Quality-Control Process:**
- **Schema Validation:** Automated scripts will verify the presence and data type of all 14 required fields.
- **Semantic Consistency:** A VLM (Vision-Language Model) will score the alignment between the `detailed image-generation prompt` and the `short image caption` to ensure logical consistency.
- **Visual Diversity Check:** Statistical analysis of `art style`, `lighting conditions`, and `camera angle` distributions will be performed per split to guarantee representation across all categories.

