### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure & Generation Strategy:**
The dataset is structured to support reproducible generative model training. We will employ a stratified sampling approach to ensure balanced representation across the 11 required visual categories. The generation strategy involves creating high-fidelity prompts using a template-based system that randomizes subject, style, lighting, and composition while enforcing uniqueness constraints to prevent semantic duplication. 

**Quality-Control Process:**
1. **Semantic Deduplication:** We will use CLIP-based embedding similarity scores to identify and remove near-duplicate prompts across splits, ensuring no leakage between Training, Validation, and Test sets.
2. **Schema Validation:** An automated script will verify that every entry contains all 14 mandatory metadata fields with valid data types and non-null values.
3. **Split Integrity:** A final audit will confirm the 80/10/10 distribution ratio and verify that file paths align with the `image_generation_dataset/{split}/images/` hierarchy.

