### Dataset Engineering Proposal

**1. Proposed Dataset Structure**
The dataset is designed for high-fidelity text-to-image generation model training, validation, and testing. It follows a strict hierarchical directory structure to ensure compatibility with standard machine learning pipelines, separating raw assets from descriptive metadata.

**Folder Hierarchy:**
```text
image_generation_dataset/
├── images/
│   ├── train/           # 80% of images
│   ├── validation/      # 10% of images
│   └── test/            # 10% of images
└── metadata/
    ├── train_metadata.jsonl
    ├── validation_metadata.jsonl
    └── test_metadata.jsonl
```

**2. Generation Strategy**
To avoid mode collapse and ensure high variance, the dataset utilizes a combinatorial attribute matrix. Prompts are engineered to cover 11 distinct visual categories (human subjects, nature, architecture, animals, objects, food, vehicles, sci-fi, digital art, abstract, and everyday life) mapped across a grid of artistic modalities, lighting schemas, and compositional rules. Each prompt is unique to prevent overfitting.

**3. Quality Control Process**
*   **Semantic De-duplication:** Using cosine similarity on prompt embeddings to ensure no two images in the same split are visually redundant.
*   **Leakage Prevention:** Strict partitioning of unique image IDs; no subject-style pair used in training will appear in validation or test splits.
*   **Label Verification:** Each entry is cross-referenced against the 14 required metadata fields to ensure zero null values and consistent formatting.

