### Dataset Strategy Overview

**Structure:** The dataset will follow a hierarchical folder structure: `image_generation_dataset/` containing subdirectories `images/`, `metadata/`, `train/`, `validation/`, and `test/`. Images will be stored in `images/` with unique UUIDs, while metadata JSONL files will reside in the split-specific folders referencing these IDs.

**Generation Strategy:** We will use a stratified sampling approach to ensure balanced representation across the 11 required categories. Prompts will be generated using a template-based system that varies artistic styles, camera compositions, and lighting conditions to prevent mode collapse. Duplicate detection algorithms (perceptual hashing) will be applied to ensure no near-duplicate images leak between training, validation, and test splits.

**Quality-Control Process:** Each entry will undergo automated schema validation to ensure all 14 required fields are present and non-empty. Human-in-the-loop review will verify prompt-image alignment and check for biased or unsafe content. Resolution and aspect ratio constraints will be enforced programmatically.

