### Dataset Engineering Strategy

**Structure & Generation Strategy:**
The dataset will be structured as a hierarchical directory system (`image_generation_dataset/`) separating raw assets from metadata. We will employ a stratified sampling approach to ensure balanced representation across the 11 specified visual categories. Prompts will be generated using a template-based system that randomizes subjects, styles, and environmental conditions while enforcing uniqueness constraints to prevent semantic duplication. The split ratio (80/10/10) will be applied at the category level to maintain distribution consistency across Training, Validation, and Testing sets.

**Quality-Control Process:**
1. **Automated Validation:** Scripts will verify the presence of all 14 metadata fields and check for format compliance (JSONL).
2. **Duplicate Detection:** Perceptual hashing (pHash) and semantic embedding similarity checks will be run to ensure no near-duplicate images exist across different splits.
3. **Human-in-the-Loop Review:** A random 5% sample from each split will be manually audited for prompt coherence, artistic style accuracy, and label precision.

