### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure**: The dataset will follow a hierarchical folder structure: `image_generation_dataset/` containing subdirectories for `images/` (raw assets), `metadata/` (centralized JSONL index), and split-specific folders (`train/`, `validation/`, `test/`) containing symbolic links or copies of images with corresponding metadata shards. This ensures clear separation for model ingestion pipelines.

**Generation Strategy**: We will employ a stratified sampling approach to guarantee balanced representation across the 11 defined visual categories. Prompts will be generated using a template-based system that randomizes subjects, styles, and environmental conditions while enforcing uniqueness constraints to prevent semantic duplication. Each entry will be assigned a split based on the 80/10/10 ratio, with a hash-based deduplication check performed on the prompt and image embedding space to prevent data leakage between splits.

**Quality-Control Process**: A multi-stage QC pipeline will be implemented: (1) Automated syntax validation to ensure all 14 metadata fields are present and correctly typed; (2) Semantic consistency checks to verify that tags match the main subject and environment; (3) Human-in-the-loop review for a 5% random sample to assess prompt clarity and artistic coherence; and (4) Visual inspection of generated prototypes to confirm alignment with specified camera angles and lighting conditions.

