### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure & Generation Strategy:**
The dataset will be organized into a root directory `image_generation_dataset/` containing subdirectories for `images/`, `metadata/`, `train/`, `validation/`, and `test/`. The generation strategy employs a stratified sampling approach to ensure the 80/10/10 split maintains category balance across all splits. We will use a deterministic hashing algorithm on the semantic embedding of the prompts to detect and prevent near-duplicate leakage between splits.

**Quality-Control Process:**
1. **Schema Validation:** Automated checks to ensure all 14 required fields are present and non-null.
2. **Semantic Diversity:** CLIP-based similarity scoring to reject prompts with >0.95 cosine similarity to existing entries within the same split.
3. **Visual Consistency:** Cross-referencing tags with the detailed prompt to ensure logical consistency (e.g., "night" lighting matches "dark" color palette).
4. **Resolution Standardization:** All entries will specify resolutions compatible with standard diffusion model architectures (e.g., multiples of 64).

