### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**Structure & Generation Strategy:**
The dataset will be structured to support reproducible generative model training. We will utilize a stratified sampling approach to ensure the 80% (Train), 10% (Validation), and 10% (Test) splits maintain distributional balance across all 11 visual categories. To prevent data leakage, we will employ perceptual hashing (pHash) and semantic embedding clustering (using CLIP ViT-L/14) to identify and exclude near-duplicate images across splits. The file hierarchy will strictly follow `image_generation_dataset/{split}/{category}/`, with parallel JSONL metadata files in `image_generation_dataset/metadata/`.

**Quality-Control Process:**
1. **Automated Validation:** Scripts will verify the presence of all 14 required fields, valid JSON syntax, and correct aspect ratio/resolution pairings.
2. **Semantic Consistency:** A cross-encoder model will score the alignment between the `detailed image-generation prompt` and the `short image caption`, flagging low-similarity pairs for human review.
3. **Diversity Check:** t-SNE visualization of prompt embeddings will ensure no single mode dominates a category.
4. **Human-in-the-Loop:** Random sampling of 5% of entries for manual verification of artistic style tags and lighting condition accuracy.

