### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

**1. Proposed Dataset Structure:**
The dataset will follow a hierarchical directory structure: `image_generation_dataset/` containing subdirectories for `images/` (organized by split), `metadata/` (containing JSONL files for each split), and specific split folders (`train/`, `validation/`, `test/`). Each entry will strictly adhere to the 14-field schema to ensure compatibility with standard diffusion model training pipelines.

**2. Generation Strategy:**
We will employ a stratified sampling approach to ensure balanced representation across the 11 required visual categories. Prompts will be generated using a template-based system combined with LLM variation to prevent semantic duplication. To ensure the 80/10/10 split integrity, we will use perceptual hashing (pHash) and CLIP embedding similarity thresholds to detect and exclude near-duplicate images across splits, ensuring no data leakage.

**3. Quality-Control Process:**
- **Automated Validation:** Scripts will verify JSON schema compliance, checking for null values in mandatory fields and valid resolution/aspect ratio formats.
- **Semantic Consistency:** A secondary VLM (Vision-Language Model) will verify that the generated prompt aligns with the assigned tags and subject matter.
- **Duplicate Detection:** Any pair of images with a structural similarity index (SSIM) > 0.95 or CLIP cosine similarity > 0.98 across different splits will be flagged for removal or reassignment.

