### Methodology Overview

As an expert AI dataset engineer, I propose the following framework for constructing your high-fidelity text-to-image dataset:

**1. Proposed Dataset Structure**
The dataset will adhere to a strict hierarchical folder structure to facilitate seamless integration with training pipelines (e.g., PyTorch DataLoader, Hugging Face datasets):
```
image_generation_dataset/
├── images/
│   ├── train/
│   ├── validation/
│   └── test/
└── metadata/
    ├── train.jsonl
    ├── validation.jsonl
    └── test.jsonl
```
This separation ensures that image files are physically grouped by split, while metadata is stored in efficient JSONL format for rapid streaming.

**2. Generation Strategy**
- **Prompt Engineering:** We will use a template-based approach with weighted tokens to ensure semantic richness. Prompts will be constructed using the formula: `[Subject] + [Secondary Objects] + [Environment] + [Art Style] + [Camera/Lighting] + [Quality Modifiers]`.
- **Split Allocation:** To prevent data leakage and overfitting, we will enforce an 80/10/10 split (Training/Validation/Testing). Near-duplicate detection algorithms (using perceptual hashing) will be run prior to splitting to ensure no near-identical compositions appear in multiple sets.
- **Category Balancing:** The generation queue will be weighted to ensure equal representation across 11 core categories: Human Subjects, Nature, Architecture, Animals, Objects, Food, Vehicles, Fantasy, Digital Art, Abstract, and Everyday Life.

**3. Quality-Control Process**
- **Automated Validation:** A pre-ingestion script will verify that every image has a corresponding metadata entry with all 14 required fields. Images with aspect ratios or resolutions deviating from the schema will be flagged.
- **Semantic Alignment Check:** We will use a CLIP-based scoring system to measure the cosine similarity between the generated image and its prompt. Entries scoring below a threshold (e.g., 0.25) will be discarded.
- **Duplicate Removal:** Perceptual hashing (pHash) will identify visual duplicates; only one instance will be retained, prioritized for the training set if unique, or validation/test if it represents a specific edge case.

