### Dataset Strategy and Quality Control

As an AI dataset engineer, my approach to building this text-to-image dataset focuses on reproducibility, diversity, and strict metadata adherence.

**1. Dataset Structure:**
The data will be organized into a hierarchical folder structure:
- `image_generation_dataset/`
  - `images/` (subfolders: `train/`, `validation/`, `test/`)
  - `metadata/` (containing `train.jsonl`, `validation.jsonl`, `test.jsonl`)

**2. Generation Strategy:**
- **Balanced Sampling:** We will enforce a quota system to ensure equal representation across the 11 specified categories (Human Subjects, Nature, Architecture, Animals, Objects, Food, Vehicles, Fantasy, Digital Art, Abstract, Everyday Life) within each split.
- **Split Integrity:** A hashing mechanism based on semantic prompt embeddings will be used to detect and prevent near-duplicate images from appearing in different splits, ensuring a clean 80% (Train), 10% (Validation), and 10% (Test) distribution.
- **Prompt Engineering:** Prompts will be constructed using a modular template: `[Subject] + [Action/Context] + [Environment] + [Style] + [Lighting] + [Camera]` to ensure high variability and descriptive richness.

**3. Quality-Control Process:**
- **Automated Validation:** A schema validator will check every entry for the presence and correct data type of all 14 required fields.
- **Semantic Consistency:** CLIP-based scoring will verify alignment between the generated prompt and the assigned tags/caption.
- **Duplicate Detection:** Perceptual hashing (pHash) will be run on the final set to guarantee no visual leakage between splits.

